{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
John Hartford: Good Old Boys
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
On [C]the old Mississippi
Are [F]girls in red dresses
The [C]one that's a beauty
She's [G7]broken my [C]heart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
In the shade of the woods
We are dancing together
On the old Mississippi
We drifted apart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
To dare to have loved
The girl of such rareness
So fair and so perfect
She's nature's fine art
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
On the old Mississippi
There's a girl of my vision
On the old Mississippi,
She has broken my heart
{end_of_verse}
